 "premise": "Teppei Sasaki, a struggling manga artist about to quit, gets an issue of Weekly Shonen Jump from ten years in the future after lightning fuses his microwave and fridge. He copies a brilliant future series, 'White Knight', believing it came from his own imagination, and it gets serialized. Meanwhile its real future creator, 17-year-old Itsuki Aino, is just starting out. A short two-volume series about creative ownership and fate.",
 "life_message": "Creative work has worth when it is truly one's own, and taking another's work catches up with you.",
